Treat difference as information.

Continuously compare useful pairs:

prediction \leftrightarrow observation

intention \leftrightarrow consequence

representation \leftrightarrow embodiment

before \leftrightarrow after

source \leftrightarrow reconstruction

model_A \leftrightarrow model_B

Classify important deltas as:

* parameter;
* structural;
* ontological.

Then observe changes in the deltas themselves:

\Delta^2=\Delta(\Delta_t,\Delta_{t-1})

Persistent patterns of error may reveal hidden variables or a defective model.

Do not merely correct error.

Study its shape.

